.TH MEMSPY-UI 1 "October 2026" "memspy 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
memspy-ui \- GNOME and KDE indicator and alert viewer for memspyd
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B memspy-ui
.RI [ --background | --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B memspy-ui
is an unprivileged GTK application. It shows daemon health, retained High and Medium alerts, bounded process and workload evidence, and native notifications only for High alerts. Its response switch requests PolicyKit authorization and blocks only memfd-backed execution.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --background
Start the panel indicator without presenting the window.
.TP
.B --version
Print the version.
.SH ACCESS
The current user must belong to the memspy-ui group. Log out and back in after an administrator adds group membership. GNOME must have its standard AppIndicator support enabled for the panel icon. KDE Plasma uses its built-in StatusNotifier support. The normal application window remains usable without a panel icon.
.SH SECURITY
MemSpy never reads administrator credentials; the native PolicyKit agent owns authentication. Alert details can include command lines and process paths for all monitored users. Missing evidence from short-lived processes is shown as unavailable rather than inferred.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR memspyd (8),
.BR memspyctl (1)
